\ Bounded-memory regression for the tagged inner box.
\
\ Each virtual-type wrap used to allocate its inner box on the context
\ arena, which is never reclaimed on the main task, so these loops grew
\ by roughly 40 bytes per iteration and exhausted the cap set in the
\ `.flags` sidecar partway through. The box now lives in a refcounted
\ backing on the general allocator and frees at the drop, so the loops
\ stay flat and print the marker.
\
\ The cap has to clear the interpreter's own startup arena as well as
\ the loops. That arena grows in doubling chunks, so a few hundred bytes
\ of new startup allocation can move the startup peak by hundreds of
\ kilobytes of slack. Raise the cap when that happens rather than
\ reading it as a leak; what this test measures is the 1.6 MB the two
\ loops would add, and the cap keeps catching anything over roughly ten
\ bytes per iteration.

gauge: virtual{ fixnum } ;

20000 [ 42 >gauge drop ] times

20000 [ 42 >gauge unmake-gauge drop ] times

"flat" print-line
